-- Test description
-- 
-- This test checks the programmability of the RX system buffer size for a
-- value of 256 bytes instead of the default 128 bytes.
-- Packet buffer size is set to 2K bytes.
--
-- This test is based on the rx_offset test which checks the default buffer 
-- size of 128 bytes
--
-- This test is intended to cover all the possible offsets from both the word 
-- boundary offsets and receive buffer offsets. This is done with frames around
-- the maximum buffer length.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
-- 
-- This test checks all four combinations of receive buffer offsets in the 
-- network configuration register, that is 0,1,2 or 3. 
-- For each receive offset value four frames are received of lengths 255, 256, 
-- 257 and 258 bytes. Receive buffers are 256 bytes long so this combination of
-- lengths will test receive buffer chaining at the end of frame.
-- These 16 combinations are then repeated four times using receive buffers 
-- starting with byte offsets of  0, 4, 8 and c. For example: 22222000,
-- 33333004, 44444008 and 0000000c.
-- A total of 64 frames will be received.
-- 
-- Detailed test description
-- 
--  1. Initialise the GEM for 100M mode operation.
--  2. Check reset state of loopback, half_duplex and extint pins.
--  3. Check reset state of registers.
--  4. Enable receive buffer and all interrupts.
-- 
--  Word offset of 0
--  ----------------
--     Byte offset set to 0 bytes, word offset set to 0 (word offset is the 
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  22222000)
--  5. Receive 255 byte frame.
--  6. Receive 256 byte frame.
--  7. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
--  8. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 1 bytes, word offset set to 0 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  22222220)
--  9. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 10. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 11. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 12. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 2 bytes, word offset set to 0 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  22222450)
-- 13. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 14. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 15. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 16. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 3 bytes, word offset set to 0 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  22222690)
-- 17. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 18. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 19. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 20. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--  Word offset of 4
--  ----------------
--     Byte offset set to 0 bytes, word offset set to 4 (word offset is the 
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  33333004)
-- 21. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 22. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 23. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 24. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 1 bytes, word offset set to 4 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  33333224)
-- 25. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 26. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 27. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 28. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 2 bytes, word offset set to 4 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  33333454)
-- 29. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 30. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 31. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 32. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 3 bytes, word offset set to 4 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  33333694)
-- 33. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 34. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 35. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 36. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--  Word offset of 8
--  ----------------
--     Byte offset set to 0 bytes, word offset set to 8 (word offset is the 
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  44444008)
-- 37. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 38. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 39. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 40. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 1 bytes, word offset set to 8 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  44444238)
-- 41. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 42. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 43. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 44. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 2 bytes, word offset set to 8 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  44444468)
-- 45. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 46. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 47. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 48. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 3 bytes, word offset set to 8 (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  44444698)
-- 49. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 50. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 51. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 52. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--  Word offset of C
--  ----------------
--     Byte offset set to 0 bytes, word offset set to C (word offset is the 
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  0000000c)
-- 53. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 54. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 55. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 56. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 1 bytes, word offset set to C (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  0000022c)
-- 57. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 58. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 59. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 60. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 2 bytes, word offset set to C (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  0000045c)
-- 61. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 62. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 63. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 64. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
--     Byte offset set to 3 bytes, word offset set to C (word offset is the
--     starting address for the buffer write i.e.  0000069c)
-- 65. Receive 255 byte frame.
-- 66. Receive 256 byte frame.
-- 67. Receive 257 byte frame (256 bytes + 1 byte).
-- 68. Receive 258 byte frame (256 bytes + 2 bytes).
-- 
-- 
-- 69. Check statistics, 64 frames received.
